**Proposition 2.3 (whole target on the full fiber).** $F(u)=R_j$ on $\Pi_j$ and $F(u)=R_0$ on all seven zero profiles. All five complete rows are attained and distinct.

Proof. This is the occurrence-sensitive target supplier NBP Proposition 9.3 and Theorem 10.4, spelled out in FCS §2. In a zero case each depth-two block is a pair of images. Its inverse retains the old pair and both cut occurrences. Injectivity of $\rho$ preserves all hidden-value equalities and disequalities, giving $R_0$. In $\Pi_j$ exactly the block at $q_j$ is $E$ and its inverse is the concrete beta leaf. Precisely its two children were born in the update. All other blocks retain their old pairs and holes. Restricting the complete occurrence partition gives (BPS.8); first positions in the remaining hole order give the name vectors. The beta at $q_j$ supplies both absent-cut guards. In particular the repeated beta partner's other occurrence remains an old hole. Deleting an entire partner class would give a different answer. The five reached supports differ, and Proposition 1.4 attains each case. $\square$

